 "stimulus_html": "<figure id=\"fig7_48\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/7f4565a474906ea6.png\" alt=\"There is a group of men on the left side of the sketch; a man in a top hat and raised stick is looking at them. On the right side of the sketch is a man at a desk with a quill; the man in the top hat looks down at him with his stick raised as if to strike the seated man.\">\n<figcaption><i>Arguments of the Chivalry</i>, 1856. About a week after the violent event depicted in the image, Henry Ward Beecher gave a speech in New York in which he proclaimed, “The symbol of the North is the pen; the symbol of the South is the bludgeon.”</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p><i>Refer to the image provided.</i></p>\n\n",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 615514,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Which of the following contradicts the statement, “The symbol of the North is the pen; the symbol of the South is the bludgeon,” in the cartoon?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1170028,
     "content_html": "Publication of the abolitionist novel <i>Uncle Tom’s Cabin</i>\n"
    },
    {
     "id": 1170027,
     "content_html": "Passage of laws in northern states refusing to enforce the Fugitive Slave Act\n"
    },
    {
     "id": 1170029,
     "content_html": "John Brown’s raid on the federal arsenal at Harpers Ferry \n"
    },
    {
     "id": 1170026,
     "content_html": "Issuance of the Emancipation Proclamation\n"
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 615515,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "The image most directly resulted from ",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1170032,
     "content_html": "the question of whether to declare war on Mexico\n"
